<title>FRANCE: French retailer Cora joins Europartners alliance.</title>
<headline>French retailer Cora joins Europartners alliance.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-05-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>French food retailer Cora said on Monday that it had joined the Europartners alliance created two years ago by Somerfield of Britain and Superunie of the Netherlands.</p>
<p>The alliance negotiates prices for its members from food suppliers internationally. Europartners estimates its members' combined 1997 turnover at 19 billion Ecus.</p>
<p>Privately owned Cora is controlled by the GMB holding company in which retail group Carrefour announced in December that it held 41.4 percent.</p>
<p>((-- Paris Newsroom, +33 1 4221 5452))</p>
